{
 "about": "MCP-19 DSN egress conformance vectors. The SAME file is in tas-mcp (internal/federation/testdata), aiqg-dashboard-be (internal/mcpconfig/testdata) and tas-mcp-servers (bridge/test). Each repo's test checks this file's sha256, so a change made in one repo fails until it is copied to all three. 'cases': 'allow' is the host:port rule (proxy, AIQG and bridge); 'resolve' + 'dial_allow' is the bridge's dial-time rule over the resolved addresses (DNS rebinding); 'registry': false cases apply only to the proxy with MCP_TENANT_SERVERS off. 'dsn_cases': a stored DSN string for tenant a, checked by AIQG at store time and by the proxy at use time (both formats). 'connection_cases': a _connection object as the bridge receives it (tenant a), with 'resolve' the DNS answer; 'allow' means the bridge dials, and then the child's DATABASE_URL must name exactly the pinned host, the port, the database and at most sslmode.",
